      "id": "angler",
      "name": "Angler",
      "description": "Round and oval lights in strings that run horizontally along the body, never singly - a string is two lights at least. The string itself is a smooth curve: it rises and falls evenly along its length rather than wandering, so the lights on it sit on a line you can follow with a finger. Each light is a pale core inside a deeper rim of the same hue, and one horse carries one design throughout. The strings turn vertical on the face and legs, where nothing else on this horse runs level. Mane, tail and hooves are untouched however close a string passes.",
